  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you run a wire from a power plant to your house, you have electricity."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But the long wire wastes power as heat and glows."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So a transformer raises it to 100,000 to 800,000 volts, and the wire cools."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But now that voltage at your house bursts into sparks."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "So a transformer on the pole steps it down."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is the power grid."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "Power flows down the wire, and the porch light comes on."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But a storm drops a branch on the line, and the lights go out."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you bury the cable underground."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "A common pole transformer turns 7,200 volts into 240."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add a meter on the wall beside the light."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built the power grid."
   }
